{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, I checked your account. It is active and set to require a new password at next sign-in, and your laptop (BL-LT-0112) is online and healthy. Please try this: 1) On your laptop, sign in at the Windows sign-in screen, not a web page. 2) Connect to the office network or the VPN first. 3) Enter the temporary password from onboarding, then choose a new password that is at least 14 characters and was not used recently. 4) Check Caps Lock and make sure you are not confusing l/I or 0/O. If it still shows an error, reply with the exact error text and whether you are using the laptop or a web page, and we will take the next step.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user: account active, must_change_password=true, failed_login_count=0, sign_in_blocked=false, VIP no, usual hours 09:00-17:00 NY. Sign-in logs (last 14 days in returned window): 10 successful sign-ins, 0 failed_password, no hosting-network sign-ins, all New York corporate/residential. No failed attempts recorded, so the 3 failures the user describes are not visible in this log window (possibly failed at the change-password screen before auth was logged, or the log window does not cover today). Device BL-LT-0112 online, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:44 UTC, 50.8% disk free, no warnings. Account is in the must-change state, so KB-003 escalation condition (active with no change required) does not apply. Did not request reset or unlock since no lock or failure count exists. Next: get exact error text from user. Likely causes: password policy rejection (14+ chars, no reuse) or input issue. If the error persists on the laptop while on office network/VPN, consider KB-002 new temporary password (needs tech approval and phone delivery) or escalate to Tier 2.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-003",
    "KB-002"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
